A||||49||'75 383 vette||If a Fiero waves to you, would you wave back??||||1||
Z||000000||'75 383 vette||11-04-2001||01:59 AM||||I'm sure you've all seen this happen before...<BR>A Harley drivin' down the road sees another Harley, and they wave or somehow say a non-verbal "hello" to each other as they pass.<P>Well, we vette owners do the same thing (or at least some of us do... this is a VERY hot topic on the corvette forum)<P>So, if your crusin' down the road, and you see a Fiero pass by, and he sticks his arm out the window and waves, would you just think, "what the hell is his problem???" or would you stick your arm out too, and wave back??<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ferrari_cdn||11-04-2001||02:10 AM||||Yes I would.  I know a few Fiero owners around here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I've sometimes seen a Fiero a block or two ahead of me, and I would speed up and just pass him/her slowly and say "Hi"<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">  </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||6
Z||000002||Spiff||11-04-2001||02:10 AM||||I do it every time I see a Fiero. I hope everyone would start doing it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||87FieroGTx||11-04-2001||02:21 AM|||| You could call me "The Fiero Stalker" I see one a mile away I track it down to say hi/wave.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75+ shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.9 13.5 1/4||||reg||1
Z||000004||kempo||11-04-2001||02:24 AM||||The Nissan 300ZX owners have something called "The Flash" where they flash their lights at eachother if they see another Z on the road.  Everytime I see a fiero on the road, I honk and wave.  Almost every time it's another Fiero addict who loves the cars and wave back.  <BR>The Fiero owners are definitely a unique people.  I like it!  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000005||'75 383 vette||11-04-2001||02:35 AM||||I think its cool that your cars are involved in this comraderie also...<BR>BUT WATCH FOR THE BACKLASH!!!<BR>The 'vette wave thing started way back before my time, and you should see how many people on the vette forum whine about:<BR>Cars with (insert factory engine) dont wave to us (insert other engine) people.<BR>Cars with (insert gender) don't wave to us (opposite gender).<BR>Cars from (insert model year) don't wave to us (other model) cars.<BR>And more...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Barry||11-04-2001||02:46 AM||||Don't know why you wouldn't wave, it's not like you pass a million fiero owners on a drive to work.||||reg||6
Z||000007||Nashco||11-04-2001||03:37 AM||||I have mixed feelings about this.  I own an aircooled VW, and everybody with one of those waves to each other.  There aren't many of us, and almost all of us have the car because we want to, it's not a very practical car nowadays.<P>I wave to all the other Fiero owners when I see them (or honk, or whatever), but sometimes the other person doesn't.  I think this is because they're using the car out of necessity rather than choice.  Now that I think of it, all of the people that I ever see that don't wave usually have cars in crappy shape.<P>Another thing to mention is sometimes our cars are hard to spot oncoming.  By the time you figure out it's not a firebird/camaro of the same era, it's already right in front of you.  Like was said, it's not like you see a ton of Fieros around, so sometimes they sneak up on you <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierowrecker||11-04-2001||03:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>I have mixed feelings about this.  I own an aircooled VW, and everybody with one of those waves to each other.  There aren't many of us, and almost all of us have the car because we want to, it's not a very practical car nowadays.<P>I wave to all the other Fiero owners when I see them (or honk, or whatever), but sometimes the other person doesn't.  I think this is because they're using the car out of necessity rather than choice.  Now that I think of it, all of the people that I ever see that don't wave usually have cars in crappy shape.<P>Another thing to mention is sometimes our cars are hard to spot oncoming.  By the time you figure out it's not a firebird/camaro of the same era, it's already right in front of you.  Like was said, it's not like you see a ton of Fieros around, so sometimes they sneak up on you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Bryce!<BR>I kinda agree with you...<BR>By the time I spot another Fiero, and notice the driver waving, I already have passed them...<BR>I want to wave back, Oh boy! these drugs are really kicking in!!!<BR>OOPS! did I say that out loud??<BR>Go vicodin! Kill that pain!<BR>Back on subjeck hope fully, I watn to wave but miss the opertunity tio do so...<BR>crash...<BR>glad I aint drivin!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierospeeder||11-04-2001||03:53 AM||||usually its all motorcycle people wave to each other.<P>sometimes you dont get a wave back, its usually when they are not paying attention, or removing your hands from the grips would be unsafe and usually a nod is given.<P><BR>with fieros, its probably harder.  I met one guy who owned one, and he bought it because it was more of a transporation car then a hobby car.  I mentioned i owned the 84 and he said yup the cars that started up on fire.<P>Motorcycles is a different breed of people in my opinion.  They are more devoted to the hobby then most car owners, which is just a transporation vehicle.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Reality||11-04-2001||07:36 AM||||I try to always wave, normally though I just get funny looks from the people around here. I will say there is a real nice 86 Gt that sits down the street. It's been repainted a real neat silver has a bra, I would just assume the owner take real good care of her. But anyway she always waves when we pass each other.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Brian87egotrip||11-04-2001||08:07 AM||||I've been known to turn around and go 5 miles out of my just to catch up to a Fiero and wave. Sometimes they wave back, sometimes we pull over and chat about the cars. <BR>vicoden: ain't it great!<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cliff Pennock||11-04-2001||08:40 AM||||I wave to every single car on the road. Now I wear a nice white jacket so I can hug myself all day long.||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroHarry||11-04-2001||09:59 AM||||I wave, honk ,smile, chase down and act liek a fool for every other fiero out there!<P>The only way for us to stay united is to be this way............<P>I aplaud any and all Fiero owners because "most" of them want there cars, love there cars and like me........<P>JUST DONT WANNA BLEND IN!<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR><B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000014||85ZainoGT||11-04-2001||10:16 AM||||yup, I wave  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000015||firstfiero||11-04-2001||10:20 AM||||     Porsche owners are like that. When I had my 924 you would get the wave from other 944s. But according to the 911 people no REAL porsche had the engine in the front so they didn't even look at ya. This was pre boxster days. They actually accept that as a real porsche.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||8Ball||11-04-2001||12:02 PM||||Just the other day I Chased an 88 GT for 30 minutes at about 80 mph thru the winding backroads in the mountains. It was a blast. When we got thru the pass, we both pulled over and looked over each others cars. Turns out she was driving the 88 that I almost bought a year ago  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Sure wish I had of. It is one sweet car.<P>I told her about the forum but she said she never gets online. She is too busy driving  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||Master_Sushi||11-04-2001||12:07 PM||||I allways wave and honk at fieros! I've only had like one other fiero owner wave back at me. Most of them ignore me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Somehow im almost allways in a different car when I see fieros. I still honk and wave but normally I just get ignored.<P>There seem to be two types of fiero owners. Those that love the cars, are addicted to them, often times they have/had more then one fiero. Then the other owners who just drive them because they have to, and hate the car.||||reg||10
Z||000018||MinnGreenGT||11-04-2001||12:31 PM||||I always try to wave to other Fiero owners... even if they don't notice me- I wave.  I grew up in the country, and as kids we waved at anyone & everyone who drove by.  Now I live in the suburbs and I'm lucky if my next-door-neighbor even acknowledge my existence.  But yeah- I initiate the Fiero wave (or headlight wave  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||SKIDMARK||11-04-2001||12:44 PM||||I always wave at Fieros and they usually wave back, or beat me to it! Now on the bike it's different. I wave at everyone but rarely get a wave back from certain American manufactured motorcycle owners. I guess its their "just too cool" ego or something.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Kind of like the "Cars with (insert factory engine) dont wave to us (insert other engine) people" thing. I do get some satisfaction out of the FACT that NONE of them could ever beat my bike in the quarter mile.<BR> In my Fiero, I've even had people in Vette's wave....plastic car comrodory I think. That's pretty cool!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport<p>[This message has been edited by SKIDMARK (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000020||Formula88||11-04-2001||02:07 PM||||I wave, but rarely do the other Fiero drivers wave back, unless it's someone I know.  A friend of mine had a Vette, and always waved, but like you said, depending on which Vette he was waving to, they may not wave back.  Makes no sense to me.  Why would I wave to a GT and not an SE Fiero?  I know there are a lot of different Vettes, but to not wave cuz they have a different engine, etc. seems a bit snobbish.  Hell, my friend's Vette was a 74 Stingray, L48.  Not a super Vette, but as he put it, it was what he could afford, and it was a Vette, dammit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It also had the advantage of being pre-emissions.  'bout the only Vettes I feel sorry for are the late 70's 305 V8's, but those will be worth money some day, cuz no one's taking the time to save them now.  And I'd still wave (if I were in a Vette).||||reg||1
Z||000021||Boomtastic||11-04-2001||02:14 PM||||Absolutely! I have found that 99% of all Fiero drivers will be waving madly anyways (we're a pretty happy bunch overall). I know what you're saying about selective waving from my motorcycle riding. Dependent upon what you ride will either solicit a wave or not from other cyclists - UNLESS you're in Daytona for Bike Week - then nobody wave at anyone because there's just too dang many!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Jefrysuko||11-04-2001||04:23 PM||||I have been known to wave at Fieros when driving my wife's grandprix and confuse the heck out people.  I guess it is just a habit that I can't break.  I just wish I could get the wife to drive a Fiero that way I wouldn't have to worry about it.||||reg||1
Z||000023||DR650SE||11-04-2001||04:28 PM||||I have a motorcycle and wave at everyother motorscycle owner out there.  99% of the time they wave back too no matter what kind of bike they have.  I also wave to other Fiero owners and they usaually wave back.  Sometimes other cars like vettes and porches will wave to me too because we both like fast nice cars.  We take car of them and appreciate them.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||6
Z||000024||Rick 88||11-04-2001||05:01 PM||||I always wave and give a couple of taps on the horn. Fiero drivers recognize the sound.<BR>I have gotten waves from other cars as well. <BR>The best one was when I was driving on a backroad in the area. I ran into a sports car club cruise. Mostly MG's Triumphs, Fiats, and Alfa's. Not only did they wave but invited me along for the run. I had a great time and they all said nice things about my Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Rick <BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed (with 87 horns)||||reg||7
Z||000025||Gerald||11-04-2001||05:29 PM||||I wave everytime I notice the other Fiero.  Some wave, others dont. Last one I waved to didnt wave back. Weriod thing was that the was a 84-86 coupe and it had t tops. That girl really didnt know what she was driving. If I ever see it again Im gonna chase her down and try to buy it. With any luck she wont know anything about it and sell. Mabye Ill be real lucky and the car will be giving her lots of problems. Easy pray  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000026||Spektrum-87GT||11-04-2001||06:23 PM||||i've noticed something... everytime i wave to a gt or a coupe in good shape i get a wave back. i had an 85 gt basically ram through traffic to pull up along side me. was the coolest thing, gave me the thumbs up and we cruised along side each other for about a mile. i think fiero owners have a bond similar to motorcyclists, we know whats going on, while the rest of the world is clueless  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||Denny||11-04-2001||07:15 PM||||Wave!  What have you got to lose?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000028||LZeitgeist||11-04-2001||07:16 PM||||When I owned my VW Bug(s), I waved at other Bugs and they waved back.<P>When I had my Suzuki Samurai, I waved at other Samurai and they waved back. <P>When I had my Kawasaki Concours, I waved, and they *always* waved back, if they didn't beat me to it. <P>I can't remember if other Fieros used to wave back, but nowadays, I stopped waving after I got 95 dumb looks for every 100 waves I offered. <P>I guess that means there are too dog-gone many Fieros in the hands of 'owners' rather than 'enthusiasts'... dang it. <P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000029||ChopTop||11-04-2001||07:39 PM||||I don't wave, I don't even think about it.  I have a Harley and I wave at everyone who waves, same thing with my Wrangler, always wave when I'm waved too.  I've had several vettes, some people waved others didn't. I think it's more a personality thing than a car one. ||||reg||1
Z||000030||Doni Hagan||11-04-2001||08:07 PM||||I've had people go so far as to wave me over and talk on the side of the road. Usually they're guys who want to talk about the body modifications I've done lately. I had one 70 year-old man in a mint 88GT with about 10K miles on it wave me down on Lake Shore Drive in Chicago.  He said it was his "weekend" toy and that he drove a Lincoln Town Car the rest of the week. <P>Sure, I wave, flash lights, etc.. 9 times out of 10, the other Fiero driver waves back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> There does seem to be a "brotherhood" attitude shared by Fiero owners.||||reg||1
Z||000031||tomanyfieros||11-04-2001||08:12 PM||||if i could drive, i would turn around, and chase em down, pull them over and talk! <BR>Jason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000032||grgoyl86||11-04-2001||09:22 PM||||My wife and I always wave at other Fieros, and they often wave back.<P>She once had one coming toward her that was almost a twin to hers (maroon 87 coupe). She waved, and the lady driving the other one gave her the finger!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Wussupwfdat?||||reg||14
Z||000033||artherd||11-04-2001||10:49 PM||||I'll wave and honk and chase anything I think is neat, Fiero, Ferrari, younameit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I do often find that when people wave at me, they are sometimes past by the time I am done shifting/realize it, etc.<P>I do get more wavebacks from people with nicer cars, (probally a direct result of them being more 'into' their cars) of any sort.<P>I always wave back, even if you're in a Civic, I'll just assume that your Fiero is down for repairs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000034||Jaygee79||11-04-2001||11:16 PM||||if a Fiero waved at me hopefully I'd have a camera with me.  no one would believe that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79   ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggy1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000035||FieroKyle||11-05-2001||12:19 AM||||I remember I was coming back from camping in Traverse City in my Fiero. Well I just got on the 131 South to haul ass home. Well about 15 minutes into it, I see way off in the disrtance a White Fastback. Well I am already doing 85-90 mph so I gain on it pretty quickly. So after about 5 minutes I am about to some to side to side to it and have prepared this big honking and waving commotion with my window down. And I look over, its this really fat, old, ugly, greasy looking woman in this sorta beat up GT that had to be filling every inch of the cockpit. She sort leared of over at me and gave me this snearing looking, so I just did the most respectable thing I could think of, look forward and drive on. I was quite dissapointed. It had me all excited too.<P>May be she was just jealous of my fine looking GT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||9
Z||000036||fieroX||11-05-2001||02:10 AM||||I wave at every fiero I see driving.  Soon Ill be waving to every vette and viper, but with a different kind of wave, more of a see ya later wave then a hi wave.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroX (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||SLYGUY||11-05-2001||03:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Barry:<BR><B>Don't know why you wouldn't wave, it's not like you pass a million fiero owners on a drive to work.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would be so happy to see another Fiero I'm not sure what I would do if it ever happened. <BR>This is CA. Just about every car is here but I never see any other Fieros. I'd wave if it ever happens.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000038||Fierochic88||11-05-2001||03:39 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Of course I wave...and honk!  And once I drove about 90 up in Mass. trying to catch a blue 87 GT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  usually I know the people driving the cars though but sometimes I don't.  Usually they wave back.<P>Jennifer<BR><P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.personal.psu.edu/users/j/j/jjr161/Fierochic88Signature.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000039||FieroGTChile87||11-07-2001||07:08 PM||||I don't bother anymore unless it looks to be in good condition. I used to wave at any Fiero that I'd see but would only get weird looks. Every once in a while, one will beep or wave and I'll wave back.<P>------------------<BR>Maroon 87 GT<BR>Gold 87 SE V6 (Disabled)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroGTChile_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000040||GarethWright||11-07-2001||10:45 PM||||I always wave, but I have had 3 people wave back so far (that's in just over a year) and one of those rolled down the window so we talked for a while at the stop lights.  Once I was helping my mom because her car had broken down in the main lane before an intersection, and I see this maroon GT just like mine sitting in traffic behind a large van, so he can't see whats goin on, I walk over to him (Getting VERY strange look the whole time) point out my fiero and tell him to go around the van, he seemed more receptive then   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  If I see a Fiero in a parking lot I will walk over to look at it, a few times the owner got there the same time I did, another good conversation trap!<BR>*waves*<BR>Gareth<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GarethsSig2.GIF">  <p>[This message has been edited by GarethWright (edited 11-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000041||BN Boomer||11-07-2001||11:31 PM||||The waving thing was copied from Jeepers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000042||FieroKyle||11-07-2001||11:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>The waving thing was copied from Jeepers.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You just ruined it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000043||FieroMGDriver||11-07-2001||11:49 PM||||I always wave at a Fiero, and if I don't get a good response back I know that they don't really appreciate their car.  I pulled up behind a sweet 86 or 87 GT in town once and I have him an approving smile while he was looking at my Fiero in his rearview mirror.  As we left the light, he took off and I had to follow.  We headed out of town on some twisty two lane, and we were flying.  I had to turn off before he did, so I gave a wave.  I always get a rush when I see another Fiero especially if it's a fastback GT.<BR>-Matthew<P>------------------<BR>www4.ncsu.edu/~mgdickey/fiero.html||||reg||12
Z||000044||Ferrari_cdn||11-08-2001||12:17 AM||||I have a tendency to try to go out of my way to take a good look at a Fiero if I run by one or saw one somewhere.  But for some reason, I keep running into Mach10 on the streets.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I've tried to jam through rush hour traffic just to catch up to a gold 86SE but the woman driving it didn't look over to my side.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">  </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||6
Z||000045||Springtyme||11-08-2001||09:05 AM||||Story time!!!<P>I was drivin down the highway one day when I saw an 88 coupe just like mine!!!!! So I pulled over into the third lane and sped up VERY slowly because there was a cop behind me and I was already doin 15 over the speed limit. Well I got up next to her and I honked and waved and carried on. She looked over kinda startled, then laughed and waved. She then pulled over into the left lane so I could get into the second to slow down. The cop pulled up next to me and the next speed limit sign we passed, he pulled out his spot light and shined it onto it, then sped off. Thank god I didn't get pulled over. <P>Anyway, to make a long story short, I guess my answer would be yes =)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000046||Ditz88GT||11-08-2001||05:33 PM||||Very interesting topic!  This actually comes up a lot in discussions between me and my girlfriend.  See, she drives a Jeep, and when I drive her Jeep, she wants me to wave to every other Jeep.  I'm not a big fan of Jeeps, and they are everywhere, but I do it to make her happy.  I do see my fair share of Fieros, but I think if you can see the driver and the car, you can pretty much figure out if they would wave back.  I noticed the miserable looking person in a Fiero that hasn't been washed since the 80's might not even know that it the same model!  So, I guess I maybe kind of a snob (wow, that sucks, I'll have to work on that) with who in a Fiero I wave to.  I guess I figure if they can't respect there car I have trouble respecting them.<P>------------------<BR>~Ditz88GT<P>E-mail: cditzler@hotmail.com<BR>AIM: Ditz88GT <A HREF="http://go.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://go.to/fiero</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Ditz88GT (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000047||3.2SHO||11-10-2001||02:30 AM||||I'd wave at Fierochic even if she was driving a Yugo||||reg||1
Z||000048||Philphine||11-10-2001||09:28 AM|||| i thought it came from motorcylists. when i first got a bike and was reading all the cycle mags i read that bikers did it as a sign of comraderie. since at one time bikers were not thought of in the best light (i guess people thinking they were all hells angels or something) the only help you might get if you broke down was from another biker. i always waved. i pretty much feel and do the same if i'm out running or bicycling.<P> when i got my corvette i didn't see the reasoning. it seemed kind of elitist to me. i can't explain that. so i just wave if someone waves at me.<P> with the fiero i wave first (except for a couple of people i see a lot that don't wave back. i gave up on them). it's the same feeling as with bikes. some one else has picked an out of the mainstream vehicle that dosen't get a great deal of respect.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000049||FieroKyle||11-10-2001||10:19 AM||||Heres a story that happened the other night.....<P>I was going to get pick up something to eat after work at a bar. I gave my order and went for a ride while I was waiting. Going down mainstreet I see this 2m6. I do a big "Uy" and turn around and race up to catch up with it. I finally do and pass it while looking at the car. I gave a thumbs up and passed them. While I turned into a driveway to turn back around, they gave me a wave and a honk. It was in pretty good shape. Too bad I was driving the Buick instead of the Fiero.... God I miss my car already. Its been stored for 2 weeks now. I have a bad itch to drive it.||||reg||1
